const e="gibfym-young-musicians-festival",u=2026,n="Read all 8 pages of the GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 (cover, important information, age groups and time limits, accompanist fees, all class tables, Rock and Pop, Gala bursaries and trophies) and both pages of the GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026. Placed: who may enter, age groups, entry limits, repeat-piece rule, how to enter, music submission, payment method, refunds, fees, accompanist, time limits and disqualification, performance-day rules, admission and safety, data protection and photographs, adjudication, medals, the Gala, all bursaries and trophies, and the class codes of each template item. Edition facts are Variables: festival and Gala dates, Gala venue, closing date, music dates, office and music contacts, every fee and every bursary or prize amount. Classes of the syllabus that the template does not carry are named in one line each under 'other': Beginners Solo, the three Local School Choir classes and the Graded Examination classes. Not copied: the organiser's bank account number and sort code are printed in the rules (rule 9); only the method is written. The documents do NOT print: the venue or street address of the class sessions (only the Gala venue John Mackintosh Hall), a phone number, the amount of the standard entrance fee for non-performers, a points scale or marks per medal (only that the British and International Federation of Festivals marking system is used), or any news or announcements. Printed differences, written as printed: the syllabus puts the Gala on Saturday 7 February in one place and Saturday 8 February in another (7 February is used because it is the last day of the festival and a Saturday); Senior is School Year 13 or under, or 18 and under on 31 August 2025, in the syllabus but aged 18 or under at the time of performance in the rules; the duet class code F is printed beside Mixed Instrumental though the key gives F as Percussion; the maximum of 60 children is printed once in rule 6 after the choir sentence and is applied to choirs. The template's age bands (4-7, 8-11, 12-15, 16-18) are the template's conversion of school years; the rows write the circular's own school-year wording. The 2026 closing dates have already passed.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Gibraltar Festival for Young Musicians (GIBFYM) 2026. Read these rules before you enter.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The festival runs from {{FestivalStartDate}} to {{FestivalEndDate}}. Entries close on {{EntriesCloseDate}}. Send the music for each piece by {{MusicDeadline}}. Questions: {{OfficeContact}}.","Notes":["Entrants must be 18 years old or under on the date of performance.","Going over the time limit means disqualification from the competition.","The complete Rules and Regulations are on the organiser's website."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The festival is for young performers. The classes are for Piano, Wind, Brass, String, Vocal, Percussion and Mixed Instrumental, in these class types: Solo, Duet, Ensemble, Choir, and Rock and Pop Solo.","Entrants play ONE piece of their own choice, up to the time set for their age group.","Backing tracks are only allowed in the Pop and Rock class. Rock and Pop pieces can only be entered in the Rock and Pop category.","All performers can ask to use the official accompanist for any class. They can also choose their own accompanist. The official accompanist is available first come, first served. Say on the entry form if you want a rehearsal with the accompanist. You are then contacted to arrange a rehearsal time.","The organiser can divide or combine classes to suit the number of entries. The committee can limit, cancel or subdivide any class.","No changes can be made to the final programme, except in exceptional circumstances.","The organiser can refuse any entry without giving a reason. It can also refuse a member of the public, or a performer, admission to any session of the festival or the Gala Concert.","Performers and accompanists are admitted free of charge for the session in which they perform. All non-performers pay the standard entrance fee.","Unaccompanied children under 16 are not admitted to the festival or the Gala Concert. Children under 16 must be accompanied by an adult.","It is not advisable to bring very young children to the adjudication days, because a quiet audience is needed for the competing performers.","Parents and teachers are responsible for the safety of young people and their belongings during the festival. Supervising adults are responsible for any injuries caused by a performer or a member of the public in their care. The festival is not responsible for loss or damage to personal property. Take special care of belongings, musical instruments and cases.","Performers should be at the venue at least 30 minutes before the advertised time of their class. An entrant who is not present when the class is called cannot take part unless a valid reason is given. The decision of GIBFYM is final.","Performers and members of the public must not enter or leave the hall once a class has started.","The audience is asked to switch off any audible device, such as watches and mobile telephones, while classes are in progress.","Names and addresses of competitors, teachers, members and helpers are stored on the festival computer and in the office files. They are used for festival purposes only and are not given to any other party. If the Administrator does not hear otherwise, it is assumed there is no objection.","There is normally a professional photographer during the festival. Photographs of competitors are published in the local media during and after the festival for promotion. If you object, tell the Administrator before the festival."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["The competition is open to any young performer aged 18 years or under on the date of performance.","Age groups follow the Education Authority School Years: Infant, Junior, Intermediate and Senior. The limit of each group is on the age group rows.","An entrant may perform only once in each class, unless playing different instruments.","An entrant may not play the same piece twice in different festival categories. A piece cannot be played at the festival more than once by the same person or group within a two-year period. The syllabus says an entrant cannot repeat a piece played in the previous two years.","In ensemble classes, an entrant may perform more than once, but with different groups of children.","Performers who are members of more than one choir may perform as a member of each choir to which they belong."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Enter","Items":["Entries must be made on the official entry form. The form is on the website, or ask for one by email at {{OfficeContact}}. Photocopies of the entry form are allowed.","The closing date for entries is {{EntriesCloseDate}}.","Send a digital copy of the music in PDF format, marked clearly with the entrant's name, class number and title of the piece, to {{MusicContact}}. This email opens for entries from {{MusicOpenDate}}. Music sent after {{MusicDeadline}} is not accepted.","Digital copies of music are allowed for this, but to follow copyright law the original must be shown at the performance.","Payment is online to the Gibraltar Academy of Music and Performing Arts. Write GIBFYM and the student's name as the reference. Cheques are not accepted.","Entry fees are non-refundable, except where a class is withdrawn because there are not enough entries."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["Solo class entry fee: {{SoloEntryFee}}. This includes the Rock and Pop Solo classes.","Duet class entry fee: {{DuetEntryFee}}.","Ensemble class entry fee: {{EnsembleEntryFee}}.","Open Choir entry fee: {{ChoirEntryFee}}.","Rehearsal with the official accompanist (15 minutes): {{AccompanistRehearsalFee}}.","Piano accompanist for each performance: {{AccompanistPerformanceFee}}."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["The festival is from {{FestivalStartDate}} to {{FestivalEndDate}}.","The Gala Concert is on {{GalaDate}}.","Entries close on {{EntriesCloseDate}}.","Music scores can be sent from {{MusicOpenDate}} and must reach the organiser by {{MusicDeadline}}."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The Gala Concert is at {{GalaVenue}}.","The syllabus and the rules do not print the venue of the class sessions."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Medals, Trophies and Bursaries","Items":["All entrants receive an adjudicator's report. First, second and third place medals may be awarded at the adjudicator's discretion.","Some winners are chosen for the Gala Concert, where the adjudicator awards trophies and bursaries.","The performers for the Gala are chosen by the adjudicator, not by GIBFYM.","The adjudicator invites 6 local performers and 6 international performers to perform and compete at the Gala for the Local Young Musician of the Year and the Best International Musician bursaries.","The Local Ensemble and Local School Choir bursaries are also decided on the final night. The top ensembles and school choirs are invited to perform.","Even if you are not invited to the Gala, you may already be a winner of one of the other bursaries or trophies.","The Local Young Musician of the Year: {{BursaryLocalYoungMusician}}.","The Best International Musician: {{BursaryBestInternational}}.","The Most Promising Local Senior: {{BursaryPromisingSenior}}.","The Most Promising Local Intermediate: {{BursaryPromisingIntermediate}}.","The Most Promising Local Junior: {{BursaryPromisingJunior}}.","The Most Promising Local Infant: {{BursaryPromisingInfant}}.","The Most Promising Lower Primary School Choir: {{BursaryLowerPrimaryChoir}}.","The Best Local School Choir: {{BursaryBestSchoolChoir}}.","The Best Local Ensemble: {{BursaryBestEnsemble}}.","Trophies: Most Promising String Instrumentalist, Most Promising Brass Instrumentalist, Most Promising Woodwind Instrumentalist, Most Promising Percussion Instrumentalist, Most Promising Piano Instrumentalist and Most Promising Vocal Instrumentalist.","Best Performance: {{PrizeBestPerformance}}."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Adjudication and Time Limits","Items":["The time limit for each class is set by age group. The programme and adjudications are scheduled precisely, so a performer who goes over time is stopped and disqualified from the competition.","The adjudicator's decision in all cases is final.","No entrant, teacher or interested party may discuss any part of the festival with an adjudicator before, during or after classes, unless the adjudicator invites it.","The adjudicator judges the performance on the day. Potential is not taken into account.","Adjudicators use a marking system set by the British and International Federation of Festivals. Marks show the quality of the performance and cover all parts of it. This helps with recommendations for special trophies.","All adjudication reports are given to the entrants at the end of each class."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Classes in the Syllabus Not Covered by This Event Setup","Items":["Beginners Solo class (class 1): for children who began taking classes from 1 September 2024. Piano, Wind, Brass, String, Percussion or Voice. One piece of your own choice. Time limit 2 minutes. Entry fee {{BeginnersEntryFee}}.","Local School Choirs (classes 6E, 7E and 8E): First School Choirs, Middle School Choirs and Senior School Choirs. Two contrasting songs, song choice open. Time limit 10 minutes. Schools may use a backing track or the official accompanist. These classes are free.","Graded Examination Classes (classes 18 to 25): own choice of piece from the ABRSM or Trinity examination syllabus, in Grade 1, Grade 2, Grade 3, Grades 4 to 5, Grade 6, Grade 7, Grade 8 and Diploma. Entry fee: {{GradedLowerEntryFee}} for Grades 1 to 3, and {{GradedHigherEntryFee}} for Grade 4 to 5, Grade 6, Grade 7, Grade 8 and Diploma."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026","Url":"https://www.gampa.gi/uploads/gibfym/GIBFYM%202026/GIBFYM%20Syllabus%202026.pdf"},{"Title":"GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026","Url":"https://www.gampa.gi/uploads/gibfym/GIBFYM%202026/GIBFYM%20Rules%20and%20Regulations%202026.pdf"}]}`),s=[],o=[{AgeGroup:"Infant",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3 (Age Groups, Time Limits); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 2",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 2 minutes in solo and duet classes. In ensemble classes it is 3 minutes."],Rules:["Infant means School Year 2 and under."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 2 minutes in solo and duet classes. In ensemble classes it is 3 minutes.

## Rules
- Infant means School Year 2 and under.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3 (Age Groups, Time Limits); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 2",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 3 minutes."],Rules:["Junior means School Year 6 and under."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 3 minutes.

## Rules
- Junior means School Year 6 and under.`},{AgeGroup:"Intermediate",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3 (Age Groups, Time Limits); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 2",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 4 minutes."],Rules:["Intermediate means School Year 10 and under."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 4 minutes.

## Rules
- Intermediate means School Year 10 and under.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3 (Age Groups, Time Limits); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 2",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 6 minutes."],Rules:["Senior means School Year 13 and under, or aged 18 and under on 31 August 2025 (syllabus).","The Rules and Regulations say Senior means aged 18 or under at the time of performance."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 6 minutes.

## Rules
- Senior means School Year 13 and under, or aged 18 and under on 31 August 2025 (syllabus).
- The Rules and Regulations say Senior means aged 18 or under at the time of performance.`}],t=[{Title:"Piano Solo",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 2A, 4A, 9A, 11A)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 2A, Junior 4A, Intermediate 9A, Senior 11A."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 2A, Junior 4A, Intermediate 9A, Senior 11A.`},{Title:"Wind/Brass/String Solo",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 2B-D, 4B-D, 9B-D, 11B-D)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 2B-D, Junior 4B-D, Intermediate 9B-D, Senior 11B-D. One class covers Wind, Brass and String."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 2B-D, Junior 4B-D, Intermediate 9B-D, Senior 11B-D. One class covers Wind, Brass and String.`},{Title:"Voice Solo",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 2E, 4E, 9E, 11E)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 2E, Junior 4E, Intermediate 9E, Senior 11E."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 2E, Junior 4E, Intermediate 9E, Senior 11E.`},{Title:"Piano Duet",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 3A, 5A, 10A, 12A)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 3A, Junior 5A, Intermediate 10A, Senior 12A.","The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 3A, Junior 5A, Intermediate 10A, Senior 12A.
- The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES.`},{Title:"Wind/Brass/String Duet",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 3B-D, 5B-D, 10B-D, 12B-D)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 3B-D, Junior 5B-D, Intermediate 10B-D, Senior 12B-D. One class covers Wind, Brass and String.","The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 3B-D, Junior 5B-D, Intermediate 10B-D, Senior 12B-D. One class covers Wind, Brass and String.
- The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES.`},{Title:"Voice Duet",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 3E, 5E, 10E, 12E)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 3E, Junior 5E, Intermediate 10E, Senior 12E.","The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 3E, Junior 5E, Intermediate 10E, Senior 12E.
- The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES.`},{Title:"Mixed Instrumental Duet",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (classes 3F, 5F, 10F, 12F)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 3F, Junior 5F, Intermediate 10F, Senior 12F.","The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["The syllabus key gives F as Percussion and G as Mixed Instrumental, but the duet classes print the code F beside Mixed Instrumental."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 3F, Junior 5F, Intermediate 10F, Senior 12F.
- The Junior, Intermediate and Senior duet classes are printed as ALL GENRES.

## Notes for participants
- The syllabus key gives F as Percussion and G as Mixed Instrumental, but the duet classes print the code F beside Mixed Instrumental.`},{Title:"Ensemble",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (classes 13A-G to 16A-G); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 6",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Infant 13A-G, Junior 14A-G, Intermediate 15A-G, Senior 16A-G. All genres."],TimeAndFormat:["Time limit: Infant 3 minutes, Junior 3 minutes, Intermediate 4 minutes, Senior 6 minutes."],Rules:["An ensemble has a minimum of 3 children and a maximum of 25 children.","An entrant may perform in more than one ensemble, but with different groups of children."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Infant 13A-G, Junior 14A-G, Intermediate 15A-G, Senior 16A-G. All genres.

## Time and format
- Time limit: Infant 3 minutes, Junior 3 minutes, Intermediate 4 minutes, Senior 6 minutes.

## Rules
- An ensemble has a minimum of 3 children and a maximum of 25 children.
- An entrant may perform in more than one ensemble, but with different groups of children.`},{Title:"Rock & Pop Solo",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.7 (classes 26, 27, 28)",Sections:{About:["Class codes: Junior 26, Intermediate 27, Senior 28. Each class is split by Voice (E), Percussion (F), Electric Guitar (H) and Bass (I).","Entrants choose pieces from the rock and pop genre or style."],TimeAndFormat:["Time limit: Junior 3 minutes, Intermediate 4 minutes, Senior 6 minutes."],Rules:["A backing track or piano may be used.","The music must be in MP3 format on a USB and must contain one instrumental track only.","All performances must be from memory."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["The emphasis is on the entrant's interpretation, music technique and performance of the piece."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class codes: Junior 26, Intermediate 27, Senior 28. Each class is split by Voice (E), Percussion (F), Electric Guitar (H) and Bass (I).
- Entrants choose pieces from the rock and pop genre or style.

## Time and format
- Time limit: Junior 3 minutes, Intermediate 4 minutes, Senior 6 minutes.

## Rules
- A backing track or piano may be used.
- The music must be in MP3 format on a USB and must contain one instrumental track only.
- All performances must be from memory.

## Judging
- The emphasis is on the entrant's interpretation, music technique and performance of the piece.`},{Title:"Open Choir",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (class 17E); GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 6",Sections:{About:["Class 17E. Open Choirs are non-school choirs."],TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 10 minutes."],Rules:["Two contrasting songs. The choice of song is open.","A choir may use the official accompanist.","A choir has a maximum of 60 children.","A performer who is a member of more than one choir may perform as a member of each choir."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Class 17E. Open Choirs are non-school choirs.

## Time and format
- Time limit 10 minutes.

## Rules
- Two contrasting songs. The choice of song is open.
- A choir may use the official accompanist.
- A choir has a maximum of 60 children.
- A performer who is a member of more than one choir may perform as a member of each choir.`}],r=[],i=[{Key:"FestivalStartDate",Kind:"date",Label:"First day of the festival",Value:"2026-02-01",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 cover and p.3 (Sunday 1st February 2026)"},{Key:"FestivalEndDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last day of the festival",Value:"2026-02-07",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 cover and p.3 (Saturday 7th February 2026)"},{Key:"GalaDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Gala Concert date",Value:"2026-02-07",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8 (Saturday 7th February); p.4 says Saturday 8th February"},{Key:"GalaVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Gala Concert venue",Value:{Name:"John Mackintosh Hall",Address:"",City:"Gibraltar",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8 (street address not printed)"},{Key:"EntriesCloseDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for entries",Value:"2025-12-05",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 cover (Friday 5th December 2025)"},{Key:"MusicOpenDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date the music email opens",Value:"2025-12-05",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.2 rule 8; GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 17 (Friday 5th December)"},{Key:"MusicDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to send the music",Value:"2026-01-12",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.2 rule 8 (Monday 12th January 2026)"},{Key:"OfficeContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Festival office",Value:{Name:"GIBFYM - GAMPA",Role:"Festival office, 7 Hospital Hill, Gibraltar",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"info@gampa.gi"},Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 cover and p.2 rule 13"},{Key:"MusicContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Email for sending the music",Value:{Name:"Miguel Monge (GAMPA)",Role:"Receives the digital music copies",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"miguel.monge@gampa.gi"},Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.2 rule 8; GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 rule 17"},{Key:"SoloEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Solo class entry fee",Value:"GBP 7 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-7 (Entry Fee column)"},{Key:"DuetEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Duet class entry fee",Value:"GBP 8 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4-5 (Entry Fee column)"},{Key:"EnsembleEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Ensemble class entry fee",Value:"GBP 10 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (Entry Fee column)"},{Key:"ChoirEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Open Choir entry fee",Value:"GBP 10 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (Entry Fee column)"},{Key:"BeginnersEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Beginners Solo class entry fee",Value:"GBP 7 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.4 (class 1)"},{Key:"GradedLowerEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Graded Examination classes, Grades 1 to 3",Value:"GBP 7 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (classes 18 to 20)"},{Key:"GradedHigherEntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Graded Examination classes, Grade 4 and above",Value:"GBP 8 per entry",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.6 (classes 21 to 25)"},{Key:"AccompanistRehearsalFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Official accompanist, 15-minute rehearsal",Value:"GBP 10 (Infant/Junior, Intermediate and Senior)",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3"},{Key:"AccompanistPerformanceFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Piano accompanist per performance",Value:"GBP 10",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.3"},{Key:"BursaryLocalYoungMusician",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Local Young Musician of the Year",Value:"GBP 500 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryBestInternational",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Best International Musician",Value:"GBP 250 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryPromisingSenior",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Most Promising Local Senior",Value:"GBP 250 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryPromisingIntermediate",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Most Promising Local Intermediate",Value:"GBP 250 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryPromisingJunior",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Most Promising Local Junior",Value:"GBP 250 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryPromisingInfant",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Most Promising Local Infant",Value:"GBP 100 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryLowerPrimaryChoir",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Most Promising Lower Primary School Choir",Value:"GBP 150 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryBestSchoolChoir",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Best Local School Choir",Value:"GBP 200 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"BursaryBestEnsemble",Kind:"prize",Label:"The Best Local Ensemble",Value:"GBP 100 bursary",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"},{Key:"PrizeBestPerformance",Kind:"prize",Label:"Best Performance",Value:"GBP 250 prize",Source:"GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 p.8"}],l=[{Claim:"Classes, age groups by school year, time limits, entry fees, accompanist fees, Rock and Pop rules, the Gala, bursaries and trophies are from the organiser's own syllabus.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own syllabus",Source:"Gibraltar Academy of Music and Performing Arts (GAMPA), GIBFYM Syllabus 2026 (8 pages)",Url:"https://www.gampa.gi/uploads/gibfym/GIBFYM%202026/GIBFYM%20Syllabus%202026.pdf"},{Claim:"Who may enter, how to enter, performance-day rules, adjudication and data protection rules are from the organiser's own rules.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules",Source:"GAMPA, GIBFYM Rules and Regulations 2026 (2 pages)",Url:"https://www.gampa.gi/uploads/gibfym/GIBFYM%202026/GIBFYM%20Rules%20and%20Regulations%202026.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:n,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:s,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:t,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:i,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,t as Competitions,l as Evidence,n as Note,a as Page,s as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,i as Variables,u as Year,c as default};
